<%# locals: (label: nil, remove_path: nil) %>
<%#
  Active-filter pill shown above tables. Two ways to set the content:
    label: "Status: Active"   → keyword arg, for plain strings
    do … end                  → block, for custom markup (sensitive spans, icons)

  Detection uses `label.present?` instead of `block_given?` because
  block_given? leaks state from outer do-blocks (e.g. when this partial is
  rendered inside `search_form_for ... do |f|`) — it can return true even
  when the current render call passed no block, which silently swallows
  the label keyword. label.present? is scope-independent: strict locals
  always populates the local with the passed keyword (or nil default), so
  this is deterministic.

  Block content takes precedence over label only when label is missing.
  Passing both is a callsite mistake — pick one.

  remove_path: omit for non-removable chip.
%>
<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-primary">
  <% if label.present? %>
    <%= label %>
  <% else %>
    <%= yield %>
  <% end %>
  <% if remove_path %>
    <%= link_to remove_path, class: "ml-0.5 hover:text-primary/70 transition-colors" do %>
      <%= render "admin/shared/icons/x", classes: "h-3 w-3" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</span>
